1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:03,800
[This series contains scenes of violence,
self-harm, and potential triggers.]

2
00:00:00,690 --> 00:00:01,800
Hey, hey, hey.

3
00:00:02,110 --> 00:00:04,860
Wake up. Stop playing dead.

4
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:05,250
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

5
00:00:07,670 --> 00:00:09,340
Hey, is he really dead?

6
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:23,390
Are you going to run away?

7
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:30,080
119, what's your emergency?

8
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:32,490
If you need help from 119...

9
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:34,170
Are you running away?

10
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:36,490
Are you planning to run away again?

11
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:41,440
What do you want from me, you bastard?

12
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:45,340
I told you I want you to sing.

13
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:46,830
Join the audition.

14
00:00:47,990 --> 00:00:49,400
I'll help you get that song back.

15
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:50,620
What right do you have to meddle?

16
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:52,470
Shouldn't you be thrilled?

17
00:00:52,770 --> 00:00:54,890
I'm giving you another chance.

18
00:00:57,770 --> 00:00:59,450
If you run away again,

19
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:01,700
it's really over.

20
00:01:02,190 --> 00:01:03,180
The end.

21
00:01:05,590 --> 00:01:06,980
You disgusting jerk.

22
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:12,010
Forget it.

23
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:16,210
Why should I waste my breath on
a criminal who snoops on others?

24
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:21,370
It's in three days.

25
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:25,320
At the Midnight Art Hall.

26
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:43,800
[Adapted from the webtoon
"The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

27
00:01:43,810 --> 00:01:46,600
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

28
00:01:46,610 --> 00:01:49,440
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

29
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,450
[Yoo Dohyun]

30
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:09,000
[Cho Chanhyeon]

31
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:10,650
[Ko Gyeol]

32
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:15,790
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

33
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:17,890
If you run away again,

34
00:02:18,770 --> 00:02:19,980
it's really over.

35
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:21,700
The end.

36
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:49,980
Ah, ah, ah.

37
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:51,940
Mic check, mic check.

38
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,400
Lee Hanyul's vocal practice session
for "Sound of Dawn"

39
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:56,700
on July 26, 2026.

40
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:58,890
Turn it off. Why are you recording?

41
00:02:59,070 --> 00:03:02,050
I'm going to sell it when you get famous.

42
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:03,940
Yeah? Then pay me before you record.

43
00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:05,940
-No, I'm broke.
-Then turn it off.

44
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:07,000
No!

45
00:03:07,150 --> 00:03:08,610
-Turn it off!
-Stay still.

46
00:03:08,810 --> 00:03:09,920
Just stay still.

47
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:11,040
Ah, ah, ah.

48
00:03:11,350 --> 00:03:14,270
I'm Adolf,
the one who wrote "Sound of Dawn."

49
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:15,880
What are you doing?

50
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:17,670
When this song becomes a hit,

51
00:03:17,670 --> 00:03:18,960
I'd become famous too.

52
00:03:19,090 --> 00:03:21,150
I'm just practicing for interviews.

53
00:03:21,150 --> 00:03:23,870
Oh my god.
You really get ahead of yourself.

54
00:03:25,090 --> 00:03:27,090
By the way, is this thing recording?

55
00:03:27,210 --> 00:03:28,430
Ah, ah, ah.

56
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:30,990
-Ah.
-Lee Hanyul!

57
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:38,720
Do you know why
I wanted to be a songwriter?

58
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:42,250
No surprise that you don't know.

59
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:46,350
After my parents passed away,
I kept having the same dream.

60
00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:52,210
In the dream, my parents
would die over and over again.

61
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:55,820
Do you remember how you'd sing to me

62
00:03:56,190 --> 00:03:58,790
every time I woke up from a nightmare

63
00:03:59,370 --> 00:04:01,710
and couldn't fall back asleep?

64
00:04:02,510 --> 00:04:04,150
Ever since then,

65
00:04:04,350 --> 00:04:06,360
every time I heard you sing,

66
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:09,740
I felt like all my worries
and sorrows vanished,

67
00:04:10,510 --> 00:04:13,170
and everything would be
safe and sound forever.

68
00:04:14,030 --> 00:04:16,209
That's why I started writing songs.

69
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:18,019
Because of you.

70
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:24,070
I wanted everyone to hear your voice.

71
00:04:25,610 --> 00:04:27,170
You're a great singer.

72
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:29,960
You got that?

73
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:34,570
So promise me that no matter
what happens, you'll keep singing.

74
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:36,670
Pinky promise.

75
00:04:38,150 --> 00:04:39,680
Come on!

76
00:05:12,450 --> 00:05:16,350
[Song Choice: Sound of Dawn]

77
00:05:20,030 --> 00:05:21,360
You've got this, okay?

78
00:05:45,330 --> 00:05:46,510
Honey water.

79
00:05:52,590 --> 00:05:53,920
What are you doing?

80
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,800
To speed up blood circulation.

81
00:05:55,810 --> 00:05:57,420
It calms your nerves.

82
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:02,650
Why are you here?

83
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:05,390
Look who's talking.

84
00:06:05,950 --> 00:06:07,560
I thought you wouldn't come.

85
00:06:07,830 --> 00:06:09,430
I didn't come for you.

86
00:06:10,630 --> 00:06:12,250
I came to get that song back.

87
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:13,640
Whatever the reason.

88
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:15,510
Good job.

89
00:06:15,790 --> 00:06:18,860
Contestants 90 to 100, please get ready.

90
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,090
Can you make it?

91
00:06:48,750 --> 00:06:50,440
I'll do my part,

92
00:06:52,830 --> 00:06:55,110
so get ready to
take that song back for me.

93
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:01,010
Wait.

94
00:07:06,570 --> 00:07:07,740
What are you doing?

95
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:13,360
Here.

96
00:07:15,230 --> 00:07:17,020
Call me if you advance.

97
00:07:17,370 --> 00:07:18,560
Good luck.

98
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:29,090
Next is Contestant 99.

99
00:07:34,810 --> 00:07:36,580
What song have you prepared?

100
00:07:39,550 --> 00:07:40,950
Sound of Dawn.

101
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:44,260
Oh. It's Herod's song.

102
00:07:44,970 --> 00:07:46,409
Adolf's song.

103
00:07:47,170 --> 00:07:48,080
Okay.

104
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:49,530
You may begin.

105
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,080
Okay.

106
00:07:53,790 --> 00:07:55,440
I'll help you get it back.

107
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:08,580
Dawn always comes softly,

108
00:08:08,730 --> 00:08:12,620
leaving secret tears behind.

109
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:14,680
The streets without you,

110
00:08:14,830 --> 00:08:16,660
the breeze without you—

111
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:21,240
why does this night seem endless?

112
00:08:21,370 --> 00:08:24,850
Just once, just this once—

113
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:31,690
if I could turn back time.

114
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,679
The sound of dawn,

115
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:38,659
my breath calling out to you.

116
00:08:39,669 --> 00:08:46,670
It may fade into the distance,
yet it still reaches toward you.

117
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:52,400
[Unspoken troubles?
Nightscape is here to listen!]

118
00:08:52,410 --> 00:08:55,180
[Click for a Private Consultation]

119
00:08:58,930 --> 00:09:00,700
Herod, come check this out.

120
00:09:01,590 --> 00:09:03,870
I went to the Super Singer audition,

121
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:07,180
and someone sang Sound of Dawn.

122
00:09:07,310 --> 00:09:09,000
His voice is crazy good.

123
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:10,630
He totally killed it.

124
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:12,050
Even better than yours.

125
00:09:12,170 --> 00:09:14,570
It's like the song was
tailor-made for him.

126
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:17,500
-Give it to me.
-Dawn always comes softly...

127
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:18,670
What do you think?

128
00:09:18,670 --> 00:09:19,700
He's insanely good, right?

129
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:22,190
Leaving secret tears behind.

130
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:25,240
Dawn always comes softly,

131
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:29,600
leaving secret tears behind.

132
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:31,540
The streets without you,

133
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:33,660
the breeze without you—

134
00:09:33,810 --> 00:09:35,990
why does this night seem

135
00:09:35,990 --> 00:09:38,180
-endless?
-Hello, Chairman.

136
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:39,390
Just once...

137
00:09:41,460 --> 00:09:43,240
Oh, it's Mr. Lee.

138
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:45,470
You're here, Boss.

139
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:48,430
I'm not the boss, but the chairman.

140
00:09:48,430 --> 00:09:49,960
Call me Chairman, you brat.

141
00:09:50,350 --> 00:09:51,710
Yes, Chairman.

142
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:58,080
Everything okay at the company?

143
00:09:58,290 --> 00:09:59,820
Are things going smoothly?

144
00:10:00,010 --> 00:10:01,480
Yes, they are.

145
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:06,100
These are the newly signed
collateral contracts.

146
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:11,280
Goodness. If they were going to
sell their kids for a few bucks,

147
00:10:11,290 --> 00:10:14,260
why did they go to all the trouble
to conceive and raise them?

148
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:15,030
[Collateral Contract
Name: Kim Jaeseok]

149
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:16,450
Don't you agree?

150
00:10:17,250 --> 00:10:18,510
Yes.

151
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,510
Sift through them.

152
00:10:20,770 --> 00:10:23,000
Keep a few useful kids here,

153
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:24,890
and transfer the rest to Mr. Han.

154
00:10:25,270 --> 00:10:26,870
Yes, noted.

155
00:10:28,180 --> 00:10:29,350
Right.

156
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:33,810
What was the name of that kid
who ran away?

157
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:36,070
Han...

158
00:10:37,250 --> 00:10:38,530
It's Lee Hanyul.

159
00:10:38,850 --> 00:10:40,250
Right, him.

160
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:42,660
Have we still not caught that kid?

161
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:45,750
Yes, sorry.

162
00:10:46,310 --> 00:10:47,680
Oh, well.

163
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:51,610
I wonder if that kid has any idea how much

164
00:10:51,750 --> 00:10:55,170
our dear Won has been suffering
because of him.

165
00:10:59,130 --> 00:11:00,310
I'll leave you to it.

166
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:04,030
Goodbye.

167
00:11:11,790 --> 00:11:16,150
[Safety Alert (Gangnam District Office)
Roads may be icy tonight. Drive slowly.]

168
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:18,810
[Delivery King: 5,000-won coupons
for regulars. Check it out now!]

169
00:11:21,860 --> 00:11:23,720
[Delivery King: A deal you can't miss!
Order now for free delivery!]

170
00:11:28,150 --> 00:11:31,100
[(Web Message) Exclusive benefits
just for you! Click the link to find out.]

171
00:11:39,960 --> 00:11:41,280
Whatever.

172
00:11:45,460 --> 00:11:47,490
Your singing still sucks.

173
00:11:47,670 --> 00:11:49,320
Don't tell me you want to be a singer.

174
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,590
Can you make it?

175
00:11:53,390 --> 00:11:55,430
What an annoying prick.

176
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,110
[Super Singer Audition Team: You have
passed the first round of auditions.]

177
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:06,000
[2026 Super Singer:
First-round audition qualifiers]

178
00:12:06,020 --> 00:12:07,430
[Lee Hanyul]

179
00:12:07,430 --> 00:12:09,900
[CEO: Lee Won]

180
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:20,520
Come in!

181
00:12:25,190 --> 00:12:26,860
Why are you so disappointed?

182
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,780
Are you waiting for someone?

183
00:12:30,920 --> 00:12:32,070
No.

184
00:12:32,350 --> 00:12:34,540
There's no way he'd come here anyway.

185
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:39,480
[Hanyul: Are you free to meet?]

186
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:46,720
You're still here?

187
00:12:47,170 --> 00:12:48,520
Leave if you're done.

188
00:12:49,010 --> 00:12:52,110
I haven't even started yet.

189
00:12:52,290 --> 00:12:53,620
Right, exactly! You...

190
00:12:53,780 --> 00:12:55,440
Why haven't you even started?

191
00:12:55,690 --> 00:12:58,530
Wait here. I have something
urgent to deal with.

192
00:13:08,650 --> 00:13:09,940
I'm busy. What is it?

193
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:11,600
Why did you want to see me?

194
00:13:11,750 --> 00:13:13,390
I passed the first round!

195
00:13:13,870 --> 00:13:14,920
So?

196
00:13:15,350 --> 00:13:16,380
Huh?

197
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:22,140
Well, I just came to tell you this.

198
00:13:22,150 --> 00:13:24,040
Then you should prepare
for the second round.

199
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:25,190
Have you decided

200
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:26,680
on a song?

201
00:13:27,060 --> 00:13:28,990
No, not yet.

202
00:13:29,900 --> 00:13:32,600
Remember the song you sang
when you delivered food to me?

203
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:34,530
The one you were humming casually.

204
00:13:35,610 --> 00:13:36,670
Sing that one.

205
00:13:37,230 --> 00:13:38,760
I'll take care of it myself.

206
00:13:38,870 --> 00:13:42,260
Sing that one. It suits your voice.

207
00:13:43,610 --> 00:13:46,800
Why are you helping me?

208
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:50,360
Are you just getting curious now?

209
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:55,080
Well... I'll tell you
if you pass the second round.

210
00:13:55,550 --> 00:13:56,490
What?

211
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:57,610
Why?

212
00:13:57,930 --> 00:13:59,310
Doubting yourself?

213
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:03,470
Well, your reason for helping me
doesn't matter anyway.

214
00:14:03,650 --> 00:14:06,180
Just be prepared to
help me get that song back.

215
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:24,220
Don't move.

216
00:14:26,770 --> 00:14:28,070
What are you doing?

217
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:33,440
This is the practice room key.

218
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:34,650
Go now.

219
00:14:35,060 --> 00:14:36,310
Focus on practicing.

220
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:40,300
Your voice comes from here.

221
00:16:17,450 --> 00:16:18,520
Hey.

222
00:16:19,390 --> 00:16:20,690
What were you doing?

223
00:16:23,350 --> 00:16:25,420
Who told you to sleep
with your mouth open?

224
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:26,820
It's bad for your throat.

225
00:16:28,930 --> 00:16:30,220
Hurry up and get ready.

226
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:31,850
You have your audition.

227
00:16:32,710 --> 00:16:33,800
Oh, right.

228
00:16:33,950 --> 00:16:35,030
What time is it?

229
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:37,550
I'll take you.

230
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:42,380
I'll speed up your blood circulation
for you on the way to help you relax.

231
00:16:42,930 --> 00:16:44,580
I'll take care of it myself.

232
00:16:45,370 --> 00:16:46,650
Alright then.

233
00:16:49,450 --> 00:16:51,520
Oh, Lee Hanyul.

234
00:16:52,850 --> 00:16:55,560
Try to nail it this time too.

235
00:16:56,660 --> 00:16:58,620
For this second preliminary round,

236
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:02,980
contestants must secure
their secret judge's approval

237
00:17:03,130 --> 00:17:05,410
to clinch a spot in the finals.

238
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:36,080
You're singing a song

239
00:17:36,230 --> 00:17:38,120
that I composed.

240
00:17:39,430 --> 00:17:41,230
You must be a fan of my songs.

241
00:17:42,590 --> 00:17:44,900
It's not me but my friend who likes them.

242
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:47,160
[Song Choice: "Summer" by Lee Won]
[Reason: It's my friend's favorite.]

243
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:49,190
Alright.

244
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:50,600
Let's hear it then.

245
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:08,520
After the rain, the scent of the schoolyard
slips through the window crack.

246
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:12,320
We pass through the damp corridor,

247
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:15,810
just walking silently all the way.

248
00:18:22,530 --> 00:18:24,570
You have a really nice voice.

249
00:18:31,290 --> 00:18:32,640
It's a no from me.

250
00:18:34,310 --> 00:18:36,440
You have a great voice.

251
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:40,080
No, it's just your voice that is good,

252
00:18:40,450 --> 00:18:42,110
nothing more.

253
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:45,730
You have zero understanding of the song.

254
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:50,750
You've overestimated
how good your voice actually is.

255
00:18:57,090 --> 00:18:58,530
You may leave.

256
00:19:15,810 --> 00:19:17,960
Try to nail it this time too.

257
00:19:19,510 --> 00:19:21,370
That jerk is unbelievable.

258
00:19:23,190 --> 00:19:24,870
Was this whole thing just to

259
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:26,700
make a fool of me?

260
00:19:31,450 --> 00:19:34,110
You're not going to break it
with your strength.

261
00:19:36,910 --> 00:19:38,130
You

262
00:19:38,700 --> 00:19:42,100
never actually planned to
help me get that song back, did you?

263
00:19:42,230 --> 00:19:44,940
You'd made up your mind to eliminate me.

264
00:19:46,890 --> 00:19:49,860
I absolutely love your voice,

265
00:19:50,350 --> 00:19:52,890
so I'm thinking of training you properly.

266
00:19:53,230 --> 00:19:55,410
I despise half-hearted people.

267
00:19:55,860 --> 00:19:57,300
Enough with your crap.

268
00:19:59,010 --> 00:20:01,050
Do you find your elimination unfair,

269
00:20:01,050 --> 00:20:02,230
or did you

270
00:20:02,610 --> 00:20:05,810
really think you could
make it to the finals at your level?

271
00:20:10,610 --> 00:20:11,720
This bodes well.

272
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:15,120
This is what the audition was for.

273
00:20:15,820 --> 00:20:18,350
You had to see how much
you were falling short.

274
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:21,670
You must be thrilled that
everything is going your way, huh?

275
00:20:21,670 --> 00:20:23,500
You really are a sickening bastard.

276
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:24,830
Nothing has changed.

277
00:20:25,540 --> 00:20:28,570
I'll help you get that song back.

278
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:31,590
You just need to keep singing.

279
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:39,820
Wait, are you sick?

280
00:20:41,030 --> 00:20:42,330
None of your business.

281
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:50,930
I'm not available now.

282
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:53,500
Let's reschedule.

283
00:20:56,060 --> 00:20:57,410
I have nothing to say to you.

284
00:20:57,410 --> 00:20:58,520
I do.

285
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:00,400
Just shut up and come with me.

286
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:09,500
Don't you want to get that song back?

287
00:21:32,150 --> 00:21:35,010
It looks like he put a lot of work
into this audition.

288
00:21:36,810 --> 00:21:37,670
Lee Hanyul.

289
00:21:37,860 --> 00:21:39,000
Get up.

290
00:21:39,030 --> 00:21:40,230
Eat something.

291
00:22:06,510 --> 00:22:08,440
Take medicine if you're sick.

292
00:22:08,610 --> 00:22:09,770
Are you stupid?

293
00:22:09,980 --> 00:22:11,550
It'll make me drowsy.

294
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:13,240
Open your mouth.

295
00:22:13,680 --> 00:22:15,410
Stop it. I'm not a child.

296
00:22:15,850 --> 00:22:18,070
If you damage your voice,
you won't hear the end of me.

297
00:22:18,070 --> 00:22:19,280
Open your mouth.

298
00:22:28,120 --> 00:22:29,090
Ah!

299
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,180
It's so bitter.

300
00:22:32,250 --> 00:22:33,370
Are you a baby?

301
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:40,700
Oh, please. Don't treat me like a kid.

302
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:45,930
You're missing out.

303
00:23:16,260 --> 00:23:17,730
What are you doing?

304
00:23:58,730 --> 00:23:59,960
You

305
00:24:00,620 --> 00:24:02,020
were different from me.

306
00:24:01,950 --> 00:24:05,430
[Seven years ago]

307
00:24:08,090 --> 00:24:11,000
Unlike me, who was sold for a few bucks,

308
00:24:11,340 --> 00:24:13,530
you lived an ordinary life.

309
00:24:18,590 --> 00:24:21,450
So I thought it was a blessing.

310
00:24:31,110 --> 00:24:32,780
After all, your voice is

311
00:24:33,270 --> 00:24:35,870
more suited to an ordinary life.

312
00:24:41,860 --> 00:24:43,630
Somewhere along the way,

313
00:24:43,810 --> 00:24:45,930
music became your dream

314
00:24:46,090 --> 00:24:48,700
and became my whole universe.

315
00:25:11,590 --> 00:25:14,420
["Sound of Dawn" by Adolf]

316
00:25:26,970 --> 00:25:28,710
[All recordings:
Hanyul's Song 32, Hanyul's Song 8]

317
00:25:41,820 --> 00:25:44,820
Somewhere along the way, your singing

318
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:47,990
became my whole universe.

319
00:25:56,030 --> 00:25:59,510
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

320
00:25:59,520 --> 00:26:00,600
Your house's been put up for rent.

321
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:01,610
What?

322
00:26:01,950 --> 00:26:03,360
It's all or nothing.

323
00:26:03,630 --> 00:26:04,580
Where are we?

324
00:26:04,750 --> 00:26:06,080
We have someone to meet.

325
00:26:06,100 --> 00:26:06,970
Who?

326
00:26:07,090 --> 00:26:08,050
Your vocal coach.

327
00:26:08,050 --> 00:26:09,050
Oh, Lee Won!

328
00:26:09,190 --> 00:26:10,680
Who's that cutie next to you?

329
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:11,610
Your boyfriend?

330
00:26:11,640 --> 00:26:12,390
Huh?

331
00:26:12,410 --> 00:26:14,080
No! What are you talking about?

332
00:26:14,080 --> 00:26:15,330
Just trust me.

333
00:26:15,490 --> 00:26:18,040
Next, we're going to play hide-and-seek.

334
00:26:18,280 --> 00:26:20,220
Eh? Hide-and-seek?

335
00:26:20,350 --> 00:26:23,050
Fight against the wind.

336
00:26:23,190 --> 00:26:24,250
Next, stage three.

337
00:26:24,440 --> 00:26:25,860
Pour your feelings into the jajangmyeon.

338
00:26:25,860 --> 00:26:26,900
What?

339
00:26:26,950 --> 00:26:29,280
You've fallen for someone before, right?

340
00:26:30,770 --> 00:26:33,590
Where is he? Where is Lee Hanyul?

341
00:26:33,880 --> 00:26:35,320
You know, don't you!
